 "text": "Hey, how's your day been so far? For oil paint, three to four weeks is usually enough if the air is fairly dry. Then touch up the corners and corners with a thin coat of lacquer just before you wrap it. That keeps the finish from getting floppy. Yes, a water based varnish dries much faster, often in a day. It's also easier to touch up. It should feel smooth to the touch, not greasy. If it does, a thin coat of lacquer repairs it.",
